From 5ddbaafe39dcd473395ddcbf9bd7f7087609da35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Barry Song (Xiaomi)" <baohua@kernel.org>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 14:49:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mm/filemap: keep the fault lock for short folio waits

filemap_fault() normally drops its mmap or VMA fault lock before waiting
for a locked folio, then retries the entire fault.  With many processes
faulting on the same resident executable or library folio, those retries
add fault-path and lock-handoff overhead without waiting for storage I/O.

When the folio is already uptodate and not under writeback, retain the
fault lock while waiting and finish in the same fault.  Keep dropping the
fault lock for non-uptodate or writeback folios, and preserve
FAULT_FLAG_RETRY_NOWAIT semantics.

Suggested-by: Matthew Wilcox (Oracle) <willy@infradead.org>
Signed-off-by: Barry Song (Xiaomi) <baohua@kernel.org>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260430040427.4672-6-baohua@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
---
 mm/filemap.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/filemap.c b/mm/filemap.c
index 9c7b3a1aa300..90421aca2a4d 100644
--- a/mm/filemap.c
+++ b/mm/filemap.c
@@ -3095,7 +3095,13 @@ static int lock_folio_maybe_drop_mmap(struct vm_fault *vmf, struct folio *folio,
 	if (vmf->flags & FAULT_FLAG_RETRY_NOWAIT)
 		return 0;
 
-	*fpin = maybe_unlock_mmap_for_io(vmf, *fpin);
+	/*
+	 * An uptodate folio which is not under writeback is likely locked
+	 * only while another fault installs PTEs.  Keep the fault lock across
+	 * this short wait so the caller can finish the fault without retrying.
+	 */
+	if (!folio_test_uptodate(folio) || folio_test_writeback(folio))
+		*fpin = maybe_unlock_mmap_for_io(vmf, *fpin);
 	if (vmf->flags & FAULT_FLAG_KILLABLE) {
 		if (__folio_lock_killable(folio)) {
 			/*
